---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const toc = [
  { id: "sec-topology", label: "01 One or many" },
  { id: "sec-partition", label: "02 Split the work" },
  { id: "sec-isolation", label: "03 Keep work separate" },
  { id: "sec-ladder", label: "04 Join the work" },
  { id: "sec-budget", label: "05 Limit per worker" },
];

const isolation = [
  {
    key: "auto",
    behavior: "Git repo → separate worktree; else temp folder",
  },
  {
    key: "git",
    behavior: "Separate git worktrees under .kineti/worktrees/<id>",
  },
  {
    key: "scratchpad",
    behavior: "Copied folders",
  },
];
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Swarm guide — Kineti"
  description="Run one worker or many workers that stay in separate folders, with a clear work split and limits per worker."
  active="swarm"
  {toc}
>
  <!-- 1. TOPOLOGY -->
  <section id="sec-topology" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-topology" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-10">
    <h2 id="h-topology" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">01</span>One or many</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">One flag picks one worker or many:</p>
    <pre class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="text-muted"># linear pipeline (default):</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti run</span> <span class="text-accent">--goal "Refactor database queries"</span> <span class="text-soft">--mode single</span>

<span class="text-muted"># parallel feature workers after ONE spec approval:</span>
<span class="font-bold text-fg">kineti run</span> <span class="text-accent">--goal "Build auth, billing, and an admin dashboard"</span> \
    <span class="text-soft">--mode swarm --cap 100</span></code></pre>
  </section>

  <!-- 2. TASK PARTITION CONTRACT -->
  <section id="sec-partition" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-partition" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-10">
    <h2 id="h-partition" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">02</span>Split the work</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      In swarm mode, steps 1–6 run once. The architecture file must list a
      <strong class="text-fg">work split</strong> — one line per worker with folder pattern and what it needs:
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto rounded-none border border-line bg-surface px-5 py-4 text-xs leading-relaxed sm:text-sm"><code><span class="text-accent">## Task Partition</span>
<span class="text-soft">- T1: database layer | scope: src/db/** ; migrations/** | deps: -</span>
<span class="text-soft">- T2: api routes     | scope: src/api/**             | deps: T1</span></code></pre>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      If two workers share files or make a loop, it goes back to step 4
      <strong class="text-fg">before any code is written</strong>. One
      <code class="text-accent">y</code> at the spec stop approves the whole split — one choice for all workers.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 3. ISOLATION -->
  <section id="sec-isolation" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-isolation" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-10">
    <h2 id="h-isolation" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">03</span>Keep work separate</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Each worker does build → review → qa in its own folder. Workers run in groups, up to
      <code class="text-accent">[execution].max_parallel_workers</code> at once:
    </p>
    <div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto border border-line">
      <table class="w-full min-w-[560px] border-collapse text-left text-sm">
        <thead>
          <tr class="border-b border-line bg-surface-2 text-xs tracking-wide text-muted">
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">SETTING</th>
            <th scope="col" class="px-4 py-3 font-normal">WHAT IT DOES</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {
            isolation.map((row) => (
              <tr class="border-b border-line transition-colors last:border-b-0 hover:bg-surface-2">
                <td class="px-4 py-3 font-bold whitespace-nowrap text-accent">{row.key}</td>
                <td class="px-4 py-3 leading-relaxed text-muted">{row.behavior}</td>
              </tr>
            ))
          }
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Each worker keeps its own log (<code class="text-accent">journal.w-&lt;task&gt;.jsonl</code>) with hashes.
      If one worker crashes, the others keep going.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 4. INTEGRATION LADDER -->
  <section id="sec-ladder" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-ladder" class="scroll-mt-20 border-b border-line py-10">
    <h2 id="h-ladder" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">04</span>Join the work</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">Joining follows fixed steps:</p>
    <ol class="mt-4 max-w-3xl list-decimal space-y-2 pl-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted marker:text-accent">
      <li>Merge workers one by one into the main folder.</li>
      <li>If files clash: try <strong class="text-fg">one</strong> auto-fix.</li>
      <li>If still clashing: stop and show the diff to you.</li>
    </ol>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      After joining, the combined code needs fresh tests before steps 10–13. Worker logs are joined to the
      main log with a two-parent record;
      <code class="text-accent">kineti merge --branch &lt;id&gt;</code> joins one branch. Orphan or late-extended
      branches block ship.
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- 5. PER-WORKER BUDGET -->
  <section id="sec-budget" data-doc-section aria-labelledby="h-budget" class="scroll-mt-20 py-10">
    <h2 id="h-budget" class="text-sm font-bold tracking-wide text-fg"><span class="mr-2 text-accent">05</span>Limit per worker</h2>
    <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
      Set <code class="text-accent">[limits].max_worker_usd</code> to limit each worker on its own. The main spend
      check already stops the total from going over; this limits one worker.
    </p>
  </section>
</DocsLayout>
